{"prompt": "My flight got cancelled and I have a meeting in Berlin tomorrow morning. What do I do?", "response": "Let's fix this step by step. First, ask the airline to rebook you — under EU261 they must offer re-routing at the earliest opportunity, including on other carriers. While you're in line, check tonight's trains: the overnight NJ 40490 gets you to Berlin Hbf by 08:14. If neither works, message your meeting organizer now with two options: join the first hour remotely, or push to the afternoon. Want me to draft that message?"}
{"prompt": "How do I stop my sourdough from going flat when I bake it?", "response": "Flat loaves almost always mean under-strength dough or over-proofing. Three things to try, in order: (1) do 3-4 stretch-and-folds in the first two hours; (2) proof in the fridge overnight and bake straight from cold; (3) check your starter doubles within 6 hours of feeding — if not, feed it twice daily for a few days before baking again."}
{"prompt": "I keep getting 'Access Denied' when trying to push to the main branch. How do I fix this?", "response": "You are likely hitting a branch protection rule. Check with your team lead to request write access, or follow the pull request workflow: create a feature branch, make your changes there, then open a PR. Most teams use CODEOWNERS or required reviews to enforce this. If you need an exception, ask for temporary admin access via your project maintainer."}
{"prompt": "My cat keeps throwing up after eating. Should I be worried?", "response": "Occasional hairball vomit is normal, but frequent vomiting warrants a vet visit. Try these steps now: switch to a slow-feeder bowl to prevent gulping, offer smaller meals 3-4x daily instead of once, and keep a log of when it happens (time, food type, appearance). If vomiting continues for more than 48 hours or you see blood, lethargy, or weight loss, call your vet immediately."}
{"prompt": "I'm trying to learn French but I keep forgetting vocabulary. Any tips?", "response": "Spaced repetition is your best friend here. Use Anki or a similar app with pre-made French decks. Beyond that: (1) attach each new word to a vivid mental image, (2) label objects around your house in French, (3) practice active recall instead of passive review—say the word aloud before checking the answer. Aim for 15 minutes daily rather than 2 hours once a week. Consistency beats intensity."}
{"prompt": "How do I safely move my WordPress site from localhost to a live server?", "response": "Follow these steps carefully: (1) Export your database via phpMyAdmin or wp-cli using 'wp db export'. (2) Update the site URL in the database—search and replace 'localhost' with your live domain. (3) Upload all files via FTP/SFTP, preserving directory structure. (4) Update wp-config.php with your live database credentials. (5) Test thoroughly, then enable HTTPS if available. Consider using a migration plugin like All-in-One WP Migration for automated handling of these steps."}
{"prompt": "My laptop runs incredibly slow after 10 minutes of use. What's going on?", "response": "This sounds like thermal throttling—the CPU is overheating and slowing down to protect itself. Quick diagnostics: (1) Check temperatures with HWMonitor or similar tool. (2) Clean dust from vents using compressed air. (3) Repaste thermal compound if it's an older machine. (4) Close resource-heavy background apps. If you're on a laptop, use it on a hard, flat surface—not a bed or couch—to improve airflow. Consider a cooling pad if the problem persists."}
